BIB                 15         33
TITLE      Measurement of 35Cl(n,p0)35S cross sections at
            0.565 MeV, 1.2 MeV, and 5 MeV with a Lithium-6
            enriched CLYC scintillator
AUTHOR     (S.Kamada, M.Hagiwara)
REFERENCE  (J,ANE,228,112065,2026)
           #doi:10.1016/j.anucene.2025.112065
INSTITUTE  (2JPNSHR,2JPNIRS)
FACILITY   (VDG,2JPNJAE) 4 MV Pelletron at Facility of Radiation
            Standards
INC-SOURCE (P-LI7) En=0.565 MeV
           (P-T)   En=1.2 MeV
           (D-D)   En=5.0 MeV
INC-SPECT  (EN-RSL-FW) Measured by BC501A liquid scintillator and
            TOF
SAMPLE     CLYC (Cs2LiYCl6:Ce) scintillator acted as a target
DETECTOR   (SCIN) Li-6 enriched CLYC scintillator (diameter
            2.54 cm, length 2.54 cm).
           (LONGC) Long counter calibrated against the national
            neutron standard at AIST
ANALYSIS   Neutron fluence measured by long counter adopted
METHOD     (PSD) Separation of neutrons and gammas
CORRECTION Neutron fluence corrected for neutron attenuation in
            CLYC scintillator evaluated by PHITS
ERR-ANALYS (ERR-T) Total uncertainty
           (ERR-S) net peak area
           (ERR-1) neutron fluence
           (ERR-2) dead-time correction
           (ERR-3) target nuclei (mass and geometry)
           (ERR-4) neutron attenuation correction
           (ERR-5) fit function for peak area
STATUS     (TABLE,,S.Kamada+,J,ANE,228,112065,2026) Tables 3+4
           (APRVD) Proofread by So Kamada (2025-12-17)
HISTORY    (20251217C) On
